Best,
Melissa

On Monday, March 15, 2021 at 2:05:01 PM UTC-4 murray...@gmail.com wrote:
> The '/' prefix on your mask covariate is a mistake. Model fits in 12 minutes when you remove it. NAs in the covariate values should be fixed somehow (maybe see ?skink example). Otherwise these are set to zero, which is not what you want.
>
> On Tuesday, March 16, 2021 at 1:36:25 AM UTC+13 melissa.e...@gmail.com wrote:
> > Hello,
> >
> > I am running a multisession model for a rabbit population that was surveyed on 2 occasions in 2018 and 2 occasions in 2019. Traps are proximity traps placed ~every 30m along transects that surveyors walked through patches each year to collect rabbit scat (genetic markers were used to determine individual rabbits from the scat). I am modeling density varying by habitat covariates, and have tried one model with D~PropDenseU (density varying by proportion of dense understory). I added the understory covariate values to mask points. This is a large dataset, with mask points covering about 300 ha. This model took ~13 hrs to run and then I received a possible maximization warning. Apologies if this is a simple question, but I would appreciate any feedback as to where I may have gone wrong with my input or code that resulted in this warning and the long run-time. Below is my code, the output, and attached are my input files. Thanks in advance, any help is very much appreciated.
> >
> > Code:
> > captures1819<- read.table("capeelizCapt.txt")
> >
> > trapfile18<- read.traps("capeeliz_proxtrap_18.txt", detector = "proximity")
> > trapfile19<- read.traps("capeeliz_proxtrap_19.txt", detector = "proximity")
> > trapfile<-list(trapfile18,trapfile19)
> >
> > #2018mask
> > mask1<- read.mask(file = "capeeliz18_mask.txt", spacing = 30)
> > covariates18 <- read.mask('capeeliz18_mask_covariates.txt')
> > mask1<- addCovariates(mask1,covariates18, strict=FALSE, replace=FALSE)
> > covariates(mask1)
> >
> > #2019mask
> > mask2<- read.mask(file = "capeeliz19_mask.txt", spacing = 30)
> > covariates19 <- read.mask('capeeliz19_mask_covariates.txt')
> > mask2<- addCovariates(mask2,covariates19, strict=FALSE, replace=FALSE)
> > covariates(mask2)
> >
> > #metapop1819mask
> > mask <-list(mask1,mask2)
> > covariates(mask)
> >
> > CHmetapop <-make.capthist(captures1819, trapfile, fmt = "XY", noccasions = 2, tol = 3, snapXY = TRUE)
> >
> > summary(CHmetapop, terse=TRUE)
> > verify(CHmetapop, report = 2)
> >
> > #V3=PropDenseU
> > metapop.fit <- secr.fit (CHmetapop, model = list(D~V3, g0~1, sigma~1), CL = FALSE, detectfn = 0, method = "Newton-Raphson", mask=mask)
