When you think about it, it's hard to distinguish the pattern of 10 dots on a map from a random (Poisson) distribution, plus you don't even know where each of those dots really is. This is radically different to a resource selection model for telemetry locations, for which you likely have a large sample and the locations are known. But of course the RSF relates to habitat selection of a different order sensu Johnson 1980.

